# ---- Stickies wall ----
#
# The wall needs a Redis store to be shared between visitors:
#
#   Vercel dashboard -> your project -> Storage -> Create Database -> Redis
#
# Connecting the store injects this for you, and `vercel env pull` brings it
# down for local dev. It is a rediss:// connection string, NOT REST
# credentials -- the store Vercel provisions does not supply KV_REST_API_* or
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_* at all, which is why this talks TCP via ioredis.
REDIS_URL=
# KV_URL and UPSTASH_REDIS_URL are accepted as aliases.
#
# Unset, `npm run dev` falls back to a JSON file in .next/cache so the page
# still works locally. That fallback is refused in production, because
# Vercel's filesystem is read-only and per-instance.

# Lets you delete ANY note, and back the whole wall up. Unset, both are
# disabled outright -- an absent token can never be matched.
#
#   openssl rand -hex 32
#
# Add it in Vercel -> Settings -> Environment Variables (Production), then
# redeploy so the running deployment can see it.
#
# Back up every note (Redis is the only copy):
#   curl -fO -J https://www.nnisalasdesign.com/api/stickies/export \
#     -H "Authorization: Bearer $STICKIES_ADMIN_TOKEN"
#
# Delete someone else's note:
#   curl -X DELETE https://www.nnisalasdesign.com/api/stickies/<id> \
#     -H "Authorization: Bearer $STICKIES_ADMIN_TOKEN"
STICKIES_ADMIN_TOKEN=
